<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Uyunid Emirate</h1><p class="st-meta">1076 CE – 1253 CE (approx.) · capital al-Ahsa</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An Arab dynasty of the Abd al-Qays tribe that ended Qarmatian rule in eastern Arabia and governed al-Ahsa and Qatif for nearly two centuries.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1076 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-allah-ibn-ali-al-uyuni">Abd Allah ibn Ali al-Uyuni</a>, a chief of the Abd al-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qays">Qays</a> tribe, rebelled against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/qarmatians-of-bahrain">Qarmatians of Bahrain</a>. With the help of a <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire</a> army he took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-ahsa-oasis">al-Ahsa</a> in 1077 and founded an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> covering the oases and coast of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-bahrain">Bahrain</a> islands.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Much of what is known comes from the poetry of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-al-muqarrab">Ibn al-Muqarrab</a>, a member of the family, and its commentary. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> controlled the date groves of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-ahsa-oasis">al-Ahsa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qatif">Qatif</a> and the pearl banks around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahrain-island">Awal</a>, the main <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-bahrain">Bahrain</a> island. It was weakened by family quarrels and lost the islands for a time to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/emirate-of-kish">Emirate of Kish</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>By the 13th century the Uyunids were reduced to a weak local power. Around 1253 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/usfurid-dynasty">Usfurid dynasty</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-amir">Banu Amir</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-ahsa-oasis">al-Ahsa</a> and replaced them.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/uyunid-emirate.jpg" alt="Uyunid Emirate" width="320" height="258"><figcaption>Image: Aziz911q8 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uyunids.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1076 CE – 1253 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>al-Ahsa</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abd Allah ibn Ali al-Uyuni</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/saudi-arabia">Saudi Arabia</a>, <a href="/countries/bahrain">Bahrain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Uyunids, Banu Uyun</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1164&amp;focus=uyunid-emirate" aria-label="Uyunid Emirate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5998 1202 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Uyunid Emirate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6318 1458L6481 1127"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6481 1127h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6318 1458h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6318 1458h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1164&amp;focus=uyunid-emirate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
